{
  "id": "docbook-xsltng",
  "area": "xslt",
  "description": "DocBook xslTNG 2.6.0 (docbook.xsl, XSLT 3.0) rendering a fixed set of 42 of its own unit-test documents to XHTML5, chosen to span size (186 B to 54 KB) and feature areas (books, sets, refentries, tables, lists, synopses, callouts, glossary, bibliography, index, footnotes, l10n, dates). go-xml gets tests/check.sh's DocBook flags except -xinclude, which no listed document needs and the warm loop cannot express. Params dc-metadata=false and generator-metadata=false drop the two outputs that differ by design: the dc.modified timestamp (current-dateTime) and the generator string (product name). Known disagreements, kept so they stay visible: dates.001 (format-dateTime [P]/[F] names, pm/friday vs p.m./Friday) and fit.001 (Saxon raises XTDE0410 in l10n.xsl, go-xml does not). Excluded: XInclude/textdata documents; l10n.001 (Saxon raises XTDE0420 that -compat-drop-attributes-on-document relaxes); table-cals.049 (1.1 MB CALS table: go-xml ~64 s, over its 60 s default -timeout, vs Saxon ~15 s cold), too slow to time repeatedly. xsltproc is omitted: the stylesheet is XSLT 3.0.",
  "inputs": "testdata/xsltng/src/test/resources/xml/",
  "normalise": "xml-c14n",
  "engines": [
    "go-xml",
    "saxon-he"
  ],
  "modes": [
    "cold",
    "warm"
  ],
  "args": {
    "go-xml": [
      "-allow-dir",
      "testdata/xsltng",
      "-allow-unparsed-text",
      "-allow-doctype",
      "-compat-drop-attributes-on-document"
    ]
  },
